<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	29.34	    +164	    28.50     29.91</p>
<p>91-Day	30.10	    +131	    29.00     30.72</p>
<p>181-Day     29.30	    + 49	    29.00     29.46</p>
<p>336-Day     28.63				27.87     28.75</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 28.41 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.19 bln pesos     2.43</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   2.01 bln pesos     2.23</p>
<p>181-Day     900 million pesos   3.36 bln pesos     3.73</p>
<p>336-Day     600 million pesos   2.45 bln pesos     4.08</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.03 compared with 3.68 the week before, on demand of 12.15 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			  57  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			  62  basis points</p>
<p>    181-Day			 16  basis points</p>
<p>    336-Day			 12  basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
</text>
